---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Nav from '../components/Nav.astro';
import '../styles/fileflex.css';
import '../styles/platform.css';
import '../styles/challenge.css';
---

<Layout
  title="The Challenge — Zero Trust Doesn't End at the Network | FileFlex Enterprise"
  description="Most security stops before it reaches the data. FileFlex Enterprise closes the access-to-data gap by applying Zero Trust principles directly to the files and folders users access — without moving your data."
>

<Nav />

<!-- ============================================================
     HERO
     ============================================================ -->
<section id="ch-hero" aria-labelledby="ch-hero-heading">
  <div class="ch-hero__content">
    <p class="ch-hero__eyebrow">The Challenge</p>
    <h1 id="ch-hero-heading" class="ch-hero__title">Zero Trust Doesn't End at the Network.</h1>
    <p class="ch-hero__title-sub">It should extend all the way to your data.</p>
    <p class="ch-hero__lede">
      FileFlex Enterprise closes the access-to-data gap by applying Zero Trust principles directly
      to the files and folders users access&mdash;without moving your data.
    </p>
    <div class="ch-hero__ctas">
      <a class="pf-btn pf-btn--lg pf-btn--uppercase" href="/platform/">Explore FileFlex Enterprise &rsaquo;</a>
      <a class="pf-btn pf-btn--lg pf-btn--uppercase pf-btn--outline" href="/demo-request/">Request a Demo &rsaquo;</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ============================================================
     ENTERPRISE DATA HAS CHANGED
     ============================================================ -->
<section class="pf-section pf-section--white" aria-labelledby="ch-changed-heading">
  <div class="pf-section__inner">
    <p class="pf-eyebrow pf-eyebrow--center">Data Sprawl</p>
    <h2 id="ch-changed-heading" class="pf-title pf-title--center">Enterprise Data Has Changed</h2>
    <p class="pf-lede pf-lede--center pf-lede--soft">
      Today's enterprise information is no longer stored in one place. It is distributed across
      Windows file servers, NAS, SharePoint, cloud storage, FTP servers and employee devices.
      At the same time, employees, customers, partners and contractors all need secure access
      to that information.
    </p>
    <p class="pf-lede pf-lede--center pf-lede--soft">
      Organizations have invested heavily in identity security, endpoint protection and Zero Trust
      Network Access. Yet the data people actually need often remains governed by legacy
      permissions and disconnected sharing tools.
    </p>
    <div class="ch-statement">
      <p>The challenge is no longer where data is stored.<br />The challenge is <strong>how access to that data is governed.</strong></p>
    </div>
    <figure class="ch-figure">
      <img
        src="/images/challenge/enterprise-data-sprawl.webp"
        alt="Enterprise Data Sprawl: employees, customers, partners and contractors all need access to enterprise data distributed across Windows file servers, NAS/SAN storage, SharePoint, Azure storage, Amazon S3, Google Cloud Storage, FTP servers and employee PCs — requiring identity verification, access control, activity logging and centralized governance."
        width="1536" height="1024" loading="lazy" decoding="async"
      />
    </figure>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ============================================================
     THE ACCESS-TO-DATA GAP
     ============================================================ -->
<section class="pf-section pf-section--light" aria-labelledby="ch-gap-heading">
  <div class="pf-section__inner">
    <p class="pf-eyebrow pf-eyebrow--center">The Missing Layer</p>
    <h2 id="ch-gap-heading" class="pf-title pf-title--center">The Access-to-Data Gap</h2>
    <p class="pf-lede pf-lede--center pf-lede--soft">
      Identity platforms verify who users are. ZTNA determines whether they can reach a network
      or application. But neither necessarily governs which individual files and folders users
      should access after they are authenticated.
    </p>
    <p class="pf-lede pf-lede--center pf-lede--soft">
      As a result, organizations often grant broader access than necessary or copy information
      into separate collaboration platforms.
    </p>
    <div class="ch-statement">
      <p>Zero Trust should extend beyond the connection and <strong>all the way to the data.</strong></p>
    </div>
    <figure class="ch-figure ch-figure--narrow">
      <img
        src="/images/challenge/zero-trust-data-layer-gap.webp"
        alt="The Zero Trust Data-Layer Gap: identity verifies users, device confirms the endpoint, network controls connections — but access is granted to the environment without governance at the file and folder level. Zero Trust Data Access closes the gap by controlling access to individual files and folders with least privilege, full governance and visibility."
        width="1024" height="1536" loading="lazy" decoding="async"
      />
    </figure>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ============================================================
     MOVING DATA ISN'T THE ANSWER
     ============================================================ -->
<section class="pf-section pf-section--white" aria-labelledby="ch-move-heading">
  <div class="pf-section__inner">
    <p class="pf-eyebrow pf-eyebrow--center">A Better Approach</p>
    <h2 id="ch-move-heading" class="pf-title pf-title--center">Moving Data Isn't the Answer</h2>
    <p class="pf-lede pf-lede--center pf-lede--soft">
      Many collaboration platforms require organizations to upload, synchronize or duplicate
      information into another repository before it can be shared. That creates additional copies
      of sensitive information, fragmented permissions, version confusion and greater
      administrative complexity.
    </p>
    <p class="pf-lede pf-lede--center pf-lede--soft">
      A better approach is to leave information where it already resides and govern access directly.
    </p>
    <div class="ch-statement">
      <p>Move <strong>governance</strong>&mdash;not data.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ============================================================
     WHY IT MATTERS
     ============================================================ -->
<section class="pf-section pf-section--light" aria-labelledby="ch-why-heading">
  <div class="pf-section__inner">
    <p class="pf-eyebrow pf-eyebrow--center">Least Privilege</p>
    <h2 id="ch-why-heading" class="pf-title pf-title--center">Why It Matters</h2>
    <p class="pf-lede pf-lede--center pf-lede--soft">
      When users receive access to more information than they need, the impact of compromised
      credentials, insider threats and ransomware can increase dramatically. Applying
      least-privilege access at the file and folder level helps reduce unnecessary exposure while
      enabling secure collaboration across existing enterprise storage.
    </p>
    <div class="ch-statement">
      <p>The goal is simple: give users access only to the information they need&mdash;<strong>and nothing more.</strong></p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ============================================================
     COMPLETE YOUR ZERO TRUST ARCHITECTURE
     ============================================================ -->
<section class="pf-section pf-section--white" aria-labelledby="ch-arch-heading">
  <div class="pf-section__inner">
    <p class="pf-eyebrow pf-eyebrow--center">The Missing Data Layer</p>
    <h2 id="ch-arch-heading" class="pf-title pf-title--center">Complete Your Zero Trust Architecture</h2>
    <p class="pf-lede pf-lede--center pf-lede--soft">
      FileFlex Enterprise extends Zero Trust to the data layer. Instead of requiring organizations
      to migrate or duplicate information, FileFlex applies centralized policies while data remains
      in its original location.
    </p>
    <p class="pf-lede pf-lede--center pf-lede--soft"><strong>With FileFlex you can:</strong></p>
    <ul class="ch-caps">
      <li>Apply least-privilege access to individual files and folders</li>
      <li>Support employees, customers, partners and contractors</li>
      <li>Control viewing, editing, downloading and sharing</li>
      <li>Keep data in existing storage</li>
      <li>Centralize governance across hybrid infrastructure</li>
      <li>Maintain complete activity logging</li>
    </ul>
    <p class="pf-lede pf-lede--center pf-lede--soft" style="margin-top: 28px;">
      FileFlex complements your existing identity, endpoint and Zero Trust investments by adding
      the missing data layer.
    </p>
    <figure class="ch-figure">
      <img
        src="/images/challenge/fileflex-architecture.webp"
        alt="FileFlex Zero Trust Data Access architecture — move governance, not data: users on laptop, tablet and mobile connect through the FileFlex Enterprise platform (policy management, administration, activity logging, policy enforcement, sharing governance and identity integration) to storage repositories including cloud storage, SharePoint and file shares. Centralized governance; data remains in place."
        width="1536" height="1024" loading="lazy" decoding="async"
      />
    </figure>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ============================================================
     ZERO TRUST DATA ACCESS — the question comparison
     ============================================================ -->
<section class="pf-section pf-section--light" aria-labelledby="ch-ztda-heading">
  <div class="pf-section__inner">
    <p class="pf-eyebrow pf-eyebrow--center">The Difference</p>
    <h2 id="ch-ztda-heading" class="pf-title pf-title--center">Zero Trust Data Access</h2>
    <div class="ch-compare">
      <div class="ch-compare__card">
        <p class="ch-compare__label">Traditional security asks</p>
        <p class="ch-compare__q">Can this user connect?</p>
      </div>
      <div class="ch-compare__card ch-compare__card--accent">
        <p class="ch-compare__label">FileFlex asks</p>
        <p class="ch-compare__q">Should this user access this specific file?</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <p class="ch-compare__note">That difference closes the access-to-data gap.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ============================================================
     FINAL CTA
     ============================================================ -->
<section id="pf-cta" aria-labelledby="ch-cta-heading">
  <h2 id="ch-cta-heading">Extend Zero Trust All the Way to Your Data</h2>
  <div class="pf-cta-buttons">
    <a class="pf-btn pf-btn--uppercase" href="/platform/">Explore FileFlex Enterprise &rsaquo;</a>
    <a class="pf-btn pf-btn--uppercase pf-btn--outline" href="/demo-request/">Request a Demo &rsaquo;</a>
  </div>
</section>

</Layout>
